          "text": [
            "If there's one thing I want you to remember about using HuggingFace pipelines, it's that you can use any of those methods on the same thread. The only difference is that you can use it on different threads, so you don't have to worry about using all of them at once.\n",
            "\n",
            "And yes, you can do that with the same code, but it's much easier. You can only do it on the same thread. And you can do it in two different threads.\n",
            "\n",
            "Now, if you're going to write something like this, you'll want to do it on a parallel thread, that you can connect to your system. If you're going to write something like this, you'll want to do it on a single thread.\n",
            "\n",
            "And that's what I'm talking about.\n",
            "\n",
            "The whole idea is that you can use a thread and then you can do something with it that you can do in parallel without having to use any of the other threads.\n",
            "\n",
            "If you've been thinking of using HuggingFace in your tests, that's totally cool. But if you've been thinking of using it in your code, you need to write the same code on different threads.\n",
            "\n",
            "And that's what I'm going to show you in the next section.\n",
            "\n",
            "And that means, you're going to need to\n"
          ]
        }
